## 24 October 2026 — cycle 5: mismatch is not necessary for the local growing modes

Completed the bounded diagnostic whose protocol was saved on 23 October; no results had been produced then. Reused hash-matched code, data and all five checkpoints from the earlier cycles without training. Computed 60 coupled local matrices: both rules, tau=1/20, full, zero-residual blocks, and additionally L=J. Primary seeds remain 0,2,3,4 and seed 1 remains a sensitivity case. No labels were used, no protocol or threshold was changed, and no new trajectory or distribution-shift test was run.

Both predeclared mode-survival gates pass in all four primary seeds in every rule/tau setting. Removing residual-weighted derivative terms changes the leading observable rate by at most 7.3343%, passing the 10% all-primary comparison. Also setting L=J changes it by up to 34.1213%, failing the quantitative gate. This rejects a requirement for parameter-derivative mismatch in these local modes. It does not establish that mismatch is irrelevant, that the replacement is a valid neural intervention, or that it explains the full nonlinear risk trajectory. Checkpoints remain nonstationary.

