## 28 October 2026 - cycle 11: a precise nonsmooth baseline and its limited scope

Executed the unchanged scalar analytic protocol saved in cycle 10. Derived stopped/full-input/cached fields from f_theta(z)=1+theta+z/4, exact student-first EMA lag/reference recurrences, and fixed-reference finite-arrival/two-cycle classification. The pointwise cached ODE with sign(0)=0 cannot be continued even as an absolutely continuous solution after reaching its attracting zero-residual boundary. An energy argument proves this obstruction. The declared Filippov inclusion instead has a unique explicit lag solution; contraction follows by monotonicity, and shared parameter velocity after contact is c/tau despite zero discrepancy.

