## 28 October 2026 - cycle 12: a faithful multivariate closure and an invented failure

Completed the unchanged cycle-11 analytic protocol. For continuous b,M and C1 finite-batch residuals, proved the exact closure b0+M0 conv(essential joint sign patterns); positive-measure zero patterns must be included. Independent intervals give an outer map. Full active-residual row rank is sufficient for equality in the actual state, by standard Paden--Sastry calculus. Added the true-partial-gradient distinction: finite-max Clarke calculus and K[grad D]=partial D make the interval velocity image exact for smooth full-input/cached rules even without rank, with frozen or continuously moving reference. These ingredients are established literature, not proposed novel theorems.

Constructed one two-output shared affine architecture with globally idempotent frozen reference: h=(1,-1), A=[[0,0],[1,1]], f_w(z)=h+w+Az. Original residual (-u,u) gives a stopped closure segment, while independent signs produce a square. The invariant u+v and nonincreasing u^2 prove unique stationary true dynamics from matched origin; pointwise discrete sign0=0 updates also remain there for all eta. The square admits a spurious path (0,t/2), zero discrepancy and risk t^2/8. Thus an incorrect model can invent predictive deterioration. Same-model full-gradient/cached interval images are exact; moving-reference residual rank is two, so this is not an EMA counterexample or a failure in the audited full-input-gradient official regression path. An all-velocities Lyapunov bound on the outer set remains conservative and sufficient.

